{"name":"Peace River","hex":"#a8bfcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Peace River","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river flowing NE in British Columbia and Alberta, Canada into the Slave River.","A river in south-west Florida, United States, that flows into Charlotte Harbor."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in northwest Alberta, Canada.","A regional district in north-east British Columbia; in full, Peace River Regional District."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Peace_River"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peace River","blocks":[{"text":"The Peace River is a 1,923-kilometre-long (1,195 mi) river in Canada that originates in the Rocky Mountains of northern British Columbia and flows to the northeast through northern Alberta. The Peace River joins the Athabasca River in the Peace-Athabasca Delta to form the Slave River, a tributary of the Mackenzie River. The Finlay River, the main headwater of the Peace River, is regarded as the ultimate source of the Mackenzie River. The combined Finlay–Peace–Slave–Mackenzie river system is the 13th longest river system in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Peace_River_Valley_Site_C_Flooding_Area.jpg/330px-Peace_River_Valley_Site_C_Flooding_Area.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_River","wikidata":"Q2220"},{"title":"Peace River (provincial electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Peace River is a provincial electoral district in Alberta, Canada. The district is mandated to return a single member to the Legislative Assembly of Alberta using the first past the post method of voting. The district used instant-runoff voting from 1926 to 1957."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Peace_River_2017.svg/330px-Peace_River_2017.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_River_(provincial_electoral_district)","wikidata":"Q7157431"},{"title":"Peace","blocks":[{"text":"Peace is a state of harmony in the absence of hostility and violence. In a societal sense, peace is commonly used to mean a lack of conflict and freedom from fear of violence between individuals or groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg/330px-Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace","wikidata":"Q454"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Peace_River_Watershed.png/500px-Peace_River_Watershed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Peace_River_Watershed.png/1280px-Peace_River_Watershed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Peace_River_Watershed.png/500px-Peace_River_Watershed.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeace_River_Watershed.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Gathering_fuel_for_the_steamship_Grenfell_on_the_Peace_River.jpg/500px-Gathering_fuel_for_the_steamship_Grenfell_on_the_Peace_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Gathering_fuel_for_the_steamship_Grenfell_on_the_Peace_River.jpg/500px-Gathering_fuel_for_the_steamship_Grenfell_on_the_Peace_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Grenfell was one of the vessels that shipped cargo on the Peace River.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGathering_fuel_for_the_steamship_Grenfell_on_the_Peace_River.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG/500px-FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG/1280px-FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG/500px-FortVermilion-Sunset.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peace River in Fort Vermilion, Alberta.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFortVermilion-Sunset.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/The_Peace_River.JPG/500px-The_Peace_River.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/The_Peace_River.JPG/1280px-The_Peace_River